{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES REQUESTED for exact clean pushed head f6335179d5b8d0e908bf4cf0bf7211d7bd79d1be and all seven cited artifacts.\n\nARCHITECTURE. The affected layers are ordinary Git storage; the application host and boundary adapter in internal/app; composition and transport in internal/service; and the surface/UI in ui plus the committed uidist. This head changes the remote-disclosure and navigation contract and updates docs/reference/architecture.md in the same head. However, the updated contract says the environment of every Git command behind the endpoint is stripped of variables that can redirect or reinterpret its reads, including the citation guard. The exact head does not preserve that stated contract because it deliberately retains arbitrary GIT_CONFIG_* command-scope configuration.\n\nSECURITY. The routing-variable and raw-delimiter repairs are sound as far as they go: all five production Git call sites use repositoryLocalGit, explicit GIT_DIR/GIT_COMMON_DIR/GIT_WORK_TREE/index/pathspec variables are removed, URL admission is an http/https allowlist at both service and href boundaries, credentials/query/fragment are refused, and the raw test closes the empty-fragment parser divergence. But inherited command-scope Git configuration can still silence the citation guard. Reproduction at this exact head: GIT_CONFIG_COUNT=1, GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0=grep.threads, GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0=-1 makes the same git grep command exit 128 with fatal: invalid number of threads specified (-1) for grep.threads. citingDocuments maps every git-grep error to nil, the same answer as no citing pages, so a cited retirement can pass. That directly violates the review condition that no inherited variable can silence the citation lookup and leaves a security-relevant fail-open path.\n\nSIMPLIFICATION. Keep one Git-command constructor, but give it a deliberately bounded environment/config contract instead of preserving arbitrary GIT_CONFIG_* input. Also distinguish git grep exit 1 (no matches) from execution/configuration errors; non-no-match failures must propagate to a refusal rather than become an empty citation set. That is simpler to reason about than enumerating more hostile config keys and preserves the requested fail-closed guard. Add a regression that injects command-scope configuration at the real citingDocuments/retirement boundary and proves the retirement is refused. The focused Go suites, npm tests (131/131), go vet, ui-check, formatting and diff checks otherwise pass; the worktree stayed clean and matched origin. Do not merge.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0aa1cf462011df2cb9cf0d900cf2de342ecca539","head":"f6335179d5b8d0e908bf4cf0bf7211d7bd79d1be","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:c36122d3cd5d3fc62652758da26b0692a09cd393\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:924a9d1399d3199a652b72427968c269f41a9f7b","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}